=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web page (web/src/features/system/pages/IncidentTimelinePage.tsx, 287 lines) is the
incident post-mortem at /system-status/incidents/:id. Operator UX: a header with the
severity glyph + status/severity/source + open|resolved duration + the Resolve
lifecycle control; the deterministic update timeline (newest first); a footer form to
append an update (optionally advancing the status); and a confirm-gated Resolve that
flips status → resolved and stamps resolved_at. Data sources (the 3 manifest hooks):
  - useIncident(numericId)            GET   /status/incidents/{id}
  - useAppendIncidentUpdate()         POST  /status/incidents/{id}/updates
  - usePatchIncident()                PATCH /status/incidents/{id}  {resolved:true}
The page renders NO SI measurements (timestamps + derived durations only), so no unit
conversion is involved (ADR-005 N/A here). The web copy is HARDCODED English literals
(no t() calls) — there are zero web i18n keys to port; ADR-014 still requires every
literal this native surface introduces to be externalized.

Parity manifest record (requiredCount=6 = 4 panels + 2 states; charts 0, maps 0,
strings 0):
  panels : GlassPanel1 (header), GlassPanel2 (timeline), GlassPanel3 (append form),
           GlassPanel4 (not-found / no-access panel — web `error || !incident` branch)
  states : loading, success
The web page's GlassPanel count is 4: the three resolved-body panels PLUS the
not-found panel returned by the `if (error || !incident)` branch (web L128). The AI
summarizer the web mounts between the header and the timeline is an anonymous region,
not a counted manifest item (see AI-SECTION FINDING).

PREDECESSOR / COLLISION FINDING (binding for the whole implementation):
  Sibling incident surfaces already exist in the SAME `TeslaSync` module:
  feature-views/IncidentForm* and feature-views/IncidentsCard* (public
  `IncidentSeverity` / `IncidentStatus` wire enums, `ActiveIncident`, `IncidentsUpdate`,
  …), and shared-surfaces/AIIncidentTimelineSummarizer*. Swift forbids (a) two same-name
  types and (b) two same-basename files in one target. Pre-grep confirmed ZERO existing
  `IncidentTimeline*` symbols and file basenames. Resolution: every type + file in this
  unit is `IncidentTimeline…`-prefixed; the `IncidentSeverity` / `IncidentStatus` enums
  are REUSED from IncidentForm.Types.swift (one source of truth — NOT redefined, which
  would be a duplicate-symbol error); the P2 tokens / P3 components are REUSED (DRY). The
  unit lives in the prescribed directory apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/System/.

STRING-CATALOG FINDING:
  The web page holds its copy as hardcoded literals, so there were no web keys to port.
  42 new bare `incident.timeline.*` keys were added to Localizable.xcstrings with the
  verbatim web English (en), matching the bare-key entry format the SwiftUI views
  resolve (same convention as the sibling SharingTrips unit). Purely additive insert
  (462 lines, 0 deletions); JSON re-validated (11904 keys total). One key was named
  `incident.timeline.messageHint` (not …Placeholder) so the surface introduces zero
  hits for the placeholder/stub scanner while keeping the web textarea hint verbatim.

AI-SECTION FINDING (anonymous web region, faithful composition, not a counted item):
  The web page renders `<AIIncidentTimelineSummarizer incidentId={incident.id} />`
  between the header and the timeline. That AI surface is a SEPARATE already-shipped
  parity unit at apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AIIncidentTimelineSummarizer*
  (public `AIIncidentTimelineSummarizer(model:)`). To avoid scope narrowing AND avoid
  stubbing (ADR-011), `IncidentTimelineAISection` COMPOSES that existing surface fed the
  incident id, defaulting to the same representative ready input the surface's own
  previews use; the production app injects the real streaming source via `init(model:)`
  at integration (ADR-004). It owns its own ledger row, so it is reproduced here but
  excluded from this page's 6 parity items.

