  IncidentTimelineRouteRegistration.swift IncidentTimelineLink + NavigationDestination + :id deep-link parser

Design notes:
  - @Observable `IncidentTimelinePageModel` consumes a KMP-bindable data-source seam
    (loadIncident ← useIncident; appendUpdate ← useAppendIncidentUpdate; resolveIncident
    ← usePatchIncident{resolved:true}); the view holds no networking (ADR-004). The
    numeric-id gate mirrors web `Number(id) > 0 ? n : null` — an invalid id resolves to
    the not-found panel without a fetch.
  - Mutations return the refreshed incident the model applies in place (web mutations
    invalidate + re-read); the sample actor appends the canonical "Incident resolved."
    line on resolve, exactly as the server does (web doc comment).
  - Adaptive macOS + iOS: ScrollView, 768pt max content width (web max-w-3xl), badge /
    control rows reflow via ViewThatFits; `.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode` is iOS-gated;
    one adaptive SwiftUI source (ADR-002/006).
  - a11y: severity glyphs hidden, panels are contain-groups, the timeline list is a
    labelled container, each row combines its children; the open-duration badge updates
    live via a per-minute TimelineView; dynamic Color.TS (light/dark/contrast), Dynamic
    Type via Font.TS, ≥44pt targets, Resolve behind an `.alert` confirm (web ConfirmDialog).
  - The page reads no SI; durations are derived from timestamps via the web fmtDuration
    port — nothing non-SI is stored or computed (ADR-005).
  - No #Preview blocks authored (this SDK's #Preview macro is ambiguous between SwiftUI
    and AppKit/UIKit — the documented baseline breakage); the Failing data-source seam
    remains for the P9 XCTest phase.

POST-REVIEW HARDENING (rubber-duck pass, all re-verified clean-compiling):
  - The AI summarizer is injectable through the page (`IncidentTimelinePage(..., 
    aiSummarizerModel:)`) so the production host wires the real gated `/ai/system/
    incidents/{id}/summarize` stream; the sample composition is the standalone/preview
    default only (ADR-004).
  - The append submit is disabled ONLY while in flight (web `disabled={isPending}`), so an
    empty-message submit reaches the "Update message is required." toast (web parity).
  - The message editor enforces the web `maxLength={4000}` via the shared `IncidentFieldBounds`.
  - The sample data source stores incidents keyed by id (no cross-route state leakage).

